<title>USA: LaCrosse Footwear to buy Pro-Trak.</title>
<headline>LaCrosse Footwear to buy Pro-Trak.</headline>
<dateline>LA CROSSE, Wis. 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>LaCrosse Footwear Inc said Wednesday it agreed to buy Pro-Trak Corp, parent of boot maker Lake of the Woods, in a deal valued at $6.5 million.</p>
<p>The agreement was a cash transaction for all of the outstanding stock of Prentice, Wis.,-based Pro-Trak and included assumed liabilities, LaCrosse said.</p>
<p>The Lake of the Woods product line has included a full range of sporting, hiking and work boots.</p>
<p>The deal was subject to normal closing conditions required to be met by both buyer and seller, LaCrosse said.</p>
<p>	   -- Reuter Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787</p>
